- Get videos with 'yt-dlp -f "mp4[height<=720]" <url>'
- Extract frames with 'ffmpeg -i data/videos/clip.mp4 -vf "fps=2" data/frames/clip\_%04d.jpg' -> every 10th frame
- label. Use CVAT or Roboflow and export in "YOLO" or "Ultralytics YOLO Detection" format. You'll need one class (gas_bottle) and a few hundred images to start. Split train/val by video, not by random frame, otherwise near-identical frames end up in both sets and your validation metrics will look unrealistically good. This is also a good point to raise in the report.
